{"n": 517, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "517.webp", "text": "TOIL\n\n3131000 REMOVING AND INSTALLING\nLEFT OR RIGHT FRONT\nSPRING STRUT ASSEMBLY\n- Four Wheel Drive -\n\nRemove front wheel - see Group 36.\nRemove ABS pulse sender - see\nGroup 61.\n\nPry out lockplate with a screwdriver.\nUnscrew collar nut.\n\nInstallation:\n\nTightening torque*.\n\nReplace lockplate, knocking It on with\nSpecial Tools 00 5 500 and 33 4 050.\n\n1?) plug for brake pad wear in-\n\nDisconnect ground lead.\n\nTake lead and brake hose out of holder\non spring strut.\n\nUnscrew push rod.\n\nInstallation:\nTightening torque\".\n\nUnscrew and suspend brake caliper\nfrom body on piece of wire.\nBrake pipe remains connected.\n\nInstallation:\nTightening torque’.\n\n* See Specifications of Gr. 31 + 34\n\n33 4038\n\n332112 |\n\n6\n\nUnscrew nut and press off tle rod joint\nwith Special Too! 32 2 070.\n\nInstallation:\n\nJournal and bore cleaned of grease.\nReplace self-locking nut.\nTightening torque*.\n\nImportant!\n\nDon't turn power steering as far as\nstop — this would damage radial oil\nseal.\n\nUnscrew nut and press off guide joint\nwith Special Tool 31 2 160.\n\nInstallation:\n\nBore and journal cleaned of grease.\nTightening torque*.\n\nLock nut with cotter pin.\n\nMount Special Tools 33 2 112/113\nwith two wheel bolts and press off out-\nput shaft.\n\ninstallation:\n\nLubricate splines of output shaft light-\nly with ofl and pull in output shaft with\nSpecial Tools 33 2 112/ 114 and\n\n33 4 038.\n\n* See Specifications of Gr. 31 + 32", "words": [["TOIL", 0.1966, 0.9668, 0.2437, 0.9788], ["3131000", 0.2695, 0.0809, 0.3207, 0.0928], ["REMOVING", 0.3283, 0.0802, 0.388, 0.0922], ["AND", 0.3921, 0.0802, 0.4154, 0.0922], ["INSTALLING", 0.4195, 0.0802, 0.4863, 0.0922], ["LEFT", 0.3283, 0.0975, 0.3556, 0.1088], ["OR", 0.3597, 0.0968, 0.3759, 0.1094], ["RIGHT", 0.3799, 0.0968, 0.4144, 0.1088], ["FRONT", 0.4184, 0.0968, 0.4564, 0.1088], ["SPRING", 0.3278, 0.1134, 0.3703, 0.126], ["STRUT", 0.3744,